  "body": "This composes PR1169's joint-entrance T37 construction with mixed local providers matched to actual idle axes. The locally verified conditional bound is **kappa = 0.001675603180601302**, **0.00205932471045090295277136174392800053609319132679508398683629385640127295304%** above PR1169's 0.001675568675201533.\n\nIn 23 of 333 calls, three additional four-helper entrance groups (619, 627, 651) use narrower entrance frames. Within-call whole-helper exchanges place the twelve affected roles in twelve distinct one-axis gaps before widening them from four to five axes. The 69 group instances consume 276 actual idle axes. All 159,840 roles remain whole; idle profile is H1=558, H48=11374. Aggregate paid delta is -828 H1 +552 H2 +276 H3 -276 H4. This changes the local provider mix and lies outside PR1169's fixed-word packing ceiling.\n\nVerification passed locally:\n- Fresh five-stage replay of the changed provider: native transport, emitted ledgers, all 704 scalar columns in both orientations, wrappers and all 2,900 exact phase edges. The unchanged provider uses the source-bound complete fresh replay retained from PR1169.\n- Unchanged pinned PR1129 provider-binding, controller, invoice and assembly engines. Strict admission rejects 114 controls, including cross-provider substitution and compensating false profiles; 12 bit and 15 controller controls also pass.\n- Independently reconstructed actual source windows, per-call width and rank recounts, all literal owners and 73-axis charts, 2,016 disjoint pending-child axis relations, and eight negative controls. Prefix 775 < 1024; physical row coefficient 17495 < 20,161.\n- Two exact moment engines and the retained 47 outer inequalities. Portable package replay passes at the stated value with explicitly reused complete native receipts and pinned parent geometry; both raw words receive independent local audits again.\n\nRun `python3 -B research/mixed-t37-entrances/verify.py --work /absolute/new/output-directory`. The default rebuilds both native providers sequentially. Optional `--base-native-from` and `--extra-native-from` explicitly reuse complete native runs with raw-word, stage and semantic bindings checked. Python 3.11+, a C++ compiler and Boost headers are required. No network or optimization solver is used. Parent geometry is archived and its source-event windows independently reconstructed; this is not a full cold ancestry rebuild. Repository-wide hosted CI is separate and has not been claimed as passing.\n\nConditional finite construction only. All-size compiler, common-label/mutable-source realization, whole-call hosting, precision/tape, exact recovery, analytic transfer, PR559 recurrence correction and PR589 bit H1-H5 assumptions remain. No unconditional theorem, full Lean certification, or global packing claim.\n\nCredits: PR1148 joint entrances, PR1129 whole-owner and admission engines, PR1131 wave ordering, PR1176 mixed-provider gap demotion, PR1169 T37 composition and all notices in the archived ancestry. PR1176's exact consulted head was 3a0d419341879a395d921693112c3b826de93677. The independent checker preserves the original predicates while selecting widths and paid profiles per call; its full diff is included. Prepared by Rohan Arun with substantial OpenAI Codex assistance, Apache-2.0.\n",
